# Docker rebuild

Docker does **not** hot-reload code changes. After editing app code, config, or assets, rebuild the image so the running container serves the latest build.

## When to rebuild

Rebuild **only at the end of a task**, and **only if**:

1. Project files were changed (not read-only Q&A or review), and
2. `npm run test:ci` completed with **all tests passing**.

Do **not** rebuild if tests failed—fix failures first, re-run tests, then rebuild.

## Command

Run this as the **last step** before ending the turn (after a green `test:ci`):

```bash
cd /Users/shaneciora/Projects/OpenLash && npm run docker:up
```

`docker:up` detects the current LAN IP for Docker when needed, then rebuilds and starts the container.

## Skip when

- Read-only task (no file edits)
- Tests did not pass
- Changes are docs-only with no runtime impact (optional skip)

If the rebuild fails, report the error; do not claim the task is done.
